# omnichannel-client — presentation boundary

This repo is the **thin Laravel shell + UI/presentation** concern (`app/Core` runtime, Filament/React surfaces, Vite assets).

## Must

- Consume addon/server contracts and APIs; do not invent backend domain state.
- Preserve existing frontend stack conventions (React/Vite/Tailwind, Filament v3, `<x-select>`, lucide-react).
- Keep `app/Addons/SeoContentAi` as compatibility shell only — no new business Models/Services/JS here.
- Peer business modules live in `seo-ops-addons` (junction `addons/` → that repo).

## Must not

- Implement backend business/domain logic that belongs in an addon.
- Silently redefine backend business rules via UI-only workarounds.
- Treat archived `D:\work-bk\omnichannel-backend` as SoT.

## When API/contract is missing

If the task needs business behavior the API does not support → **report the backend/addon requirement**; do not embed domain rules in the client.

